nkType":"web"},"range":{"length":18,"start":162},"type":"link"},{"URL":"https://www.eatingwell.com/anti-inflammatory-diet-recipes-8660050","analytics":{"linkType":"web"},"range":{"length":25,"start":185},"type":"link"}],"identifier":"_anf-body-356","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":531,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"},{"range":{"length":531,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"}],"layout":"calloutBodyLayout-ComponentLayout-1","role":"body","text":"Yes, meal plans are meant to be enjoyed so feel free to modify if there’s a meal you don’t like. You could repeat a meal in this plan or browse some of our other Mediterranean diet and anti-Inflammatory recipes for additional inspiration. In this plan, we included recipes that align with the principles of the Mediterranean diet and anti-inflammatory diet and chose recipes without any added sugar. We aimed for a minimum of 60 grams of protein and 30 grams of fiber per day, though most days came in quite a bit higher than that.","textStyle":"faqAnswerStyle","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-heading3-96","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":48,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-106"},{"range":{"length":48,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-106"}],"layout":"faqQuestionLayout-ComponentLayout-1","role":"heading3","text":"Can I eat the same breakfast or lunch every day?","textStyle":"faqQuestionStyle","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-357","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":411,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"},{"range":{"length":411,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"}],"layout":"calloutBodyLayout-ComponentLayout-1","role":"body","text":"If you prefer to eat the same breakfast and lunch every day, go for it! Each recipe aligns with the principles of Mediterranean and anti-inflammatory diets while skipping added sugar, the calories do range a little. Each breakfast ranges from 296 to 499 calories while the lunches span 405 to 744 calories. If you’re closely monitoring calories or other nutrients, you may want to be mindful when making a swap.","textStyle":"faqAnswerStyle","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-heading3-97","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":51,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-106"},{"range":{"length":51,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-106"}],"layout":"faqQuestionLayout-ComponentLayout-1","role":"heading3","text":"Why is there not a modification for 1,200 calories?","textStyle":"faqQuestionStyle","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-358","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":293,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"},{"range":{"length":293,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"}],"layout":"calloutBodyLayout-ComponentLayout-1","role":"body","text":"We no longer provide modifications for 1,200-calorie days in our meal plans. The 2020-2025 Dietary Guidelines for Americans suggests that limiting calories to 1,200 per day is too low for most people to meet their nutritional needs, plus it’s unsustainable for long-term health and well-being.","textStyle":"faqAnswerStyle","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-heading3-98","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":54,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-106"},{"range":{"length":54,"start":0},"textStyle":"_anf-ts-106"}],"layout":"faqQuestionLayout-ComponentLayout-1","role":"heading3","text":"What’s the difference between added and natural sugar?","textStyle":"faqQuestionStyle","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-359","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":384,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"},{"range":{"length":384,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"}],"layout":"calloutBodyLayout-ComponentLayout-1","role":"body","text":"Added sugars are those added during food processing to increase sweetness or palatability. Natural sugars refers to those that are naturally occurring in foods like unsweetened dairy, fruits and vegetables. Because natural sugars are found in foods that offer nutrients like protein or fiber as well as vitamins and minerals, they don’t have the same impact on health as added sugars.","textStyle":"faqAnswerStyle","type":"text"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-143","layout":"calloutComponetLayout","role":"container","style":"faqComponentStyle","type":"container"},{"identifier":"_anf-heading2-6","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":41,"start":0},"textStyle":"nutrient-major"},{"range":{"length":41,"start":0},"textStyle":"nutrient-major"}],"layout":"heading2Layout","role":"heading2","text":"Health Benefits of the Mediterranean Diet","type":"text"},{"additions":[{"URL":"https://apple.news/AymOExb9rQaOyDH8oxECEmA","analytics":{"linkType":"web"},"range":{"length":18,"start":42},"type":"link"}],"identifier":"_anf-body-211","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":1233,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"},{"range":{"length":1233,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"}],"layout":"fromTheEditorsTextLayout","role":"body","text":"Health experts continuously recognize the Mediterranean diet as one of the healthiest ways of eating. It’s flexible, so it can be followed long-term and doesn’t explicitly restrict any food groups entirely. It emphasizes a high intake of plant-based foods, like fruits, vegetables, whole grains and legumes, as well as healthy fats from nuts, olive oil, avocado, seeds and fish and a wide variety of protein sources. It also encourages cooking more meals at home and sharing meals with others. The Mediterranean diet and the anti-inflammatory diet are very similar. The anti-inflammatory diet emphasizes many of the same foods but specifically prioritizes foods rich in nutrients that are linked to reduced inflammation, such as fiber, omega-3 fatty acids, zinc, polyphenols and vitamins C and E. While the Mediterranean diet gets a lot of praise, it’s certainly well-deserved. Research links the Mediterranean diet with a reduced risk of developing type 2 diabetes, obesity, heart disease, cognitive decline and even certain cancers. It’s important to note that while the Mediterranean diet is named after the region in which it was first studied in the 1960s, this way of eating is adaptable to a variety of cuisines and cultures. ","type":"text"},{"allowAutoplacedAds":false,"components":[{"identifier":"_anf-heading3-99","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":24,"start":0},"textStyle":"nutrient-major"}],"layout":"calloutHeadingLayout-ComponentLayout-1","role":"heading3","text":"How We Create Meal Plans","textStyle":"calloutHeadingTextStyle","type":"text"},{"identifier":"_anf-body-360","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":423,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"},{"range":{"length":423,"start":0},"textStyle":"default-tag-star-rating-number"}],"layout":"calloutBodyLayout-ComponentLayout-1","role":"body","text":"Registered dietitians thoughtfully create EatingWell’s meal plans to be easy-to-follow and delicious. Each meal plan meets specific parameters depending on the health condition and/or lifestyle goal it is targeting and is analyzed for accuracy using the nutrition database, ESHA Food Processor. As nutritional needs differ from person to person, we encourage you to use these plans as inspiration and adjust as you see fit.","textStyle":"calloutBodyTextStyle","type":"text"}],"identifier":"_anf-container-144","layout":"calloutComponetLayout","role":"container","style":"calloutComponentStyle","type":"container"},{"allowAutoplacedAds":true,"components":[{"identifier":"_anf-heading3-100","inlineTextStyles":[{"range":{"length":10,"start":0},"textStyle":"nutrient-major"}],"layout":"recircHeadingLayout","role":"heading3","text":"Dig Deeper","textStyle":"calloutHeadingTextStyle","type":"text"},{"components":[{"components":[{"identifier":"_anf-image-61","imageIdentifier":"8dad1dd420a8e66300d2b0c03684a176","layout":"_defaultComponentLayout","role":"image","type":"image"},{"components":[{"additions":[{"URL":"https://apple.news/A7f-1X